{"name":"Baby Talk Grey","hex":"#bababa","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"talk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To communicate, usually by means of speech.","To discuss; to talk about."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conversation or discussion; usually serious, but informal.","A lecture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talk"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baby talk","blocks":[{"text":"Baby talk or child-directed speech (CDS) is a type of speech associated with an older person speaking to an infant, toddler or very young child. CDS is characterized by a \"sing song\" pattern of intonation that differentiates it from the more monotone style used with other adults, e.g., CDS has higher and wider pitch, slower speech rate and shorter utterances."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_talk"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain